1	//! This contract implements a proxy that gets the implementation address for
2	//! each call from an [`UpgradeableBeacon`][UpgradeableBeacon].
3	//!
4	//! The beacon address can only be set once during construction, and cannot be
5	//! changed afterwards. It is stored in an immutable variable to avoid
6	//! unnecessary storage reads, and also in the beacon storage slot specified by
7	//! [ERC-1967] so that it can be accessed externally.
8	//!
9	//! CAUTION: Since the beacon address can never be changed, you must ensure that
10	//! you either control the beacon, or trust the beacon to not upgrade the
11	//! implementation maliciously.
12	//!
13	//! IMPORTANT: Do not use the implementation logic to modify the beacon storage
14	//! slot. Doing so would leave the proxy in an inconsistent state where the
15	//! beacon storage slot does not match the beacon address.
16	//!
17	//! [UpgradeableBeacon]: super::UpgradeableBeacon
18	//! [ERC-1967]: https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-1967
19	
20	use alloc::{vec, vec::Vec};
